lines += ['', '**Observed total: 65 pass, 0 fail, 0 not-run on the prepared VMs.** This is a scripted outcome pass, not Tier 1 driver acceptance or full release/memory acceptance. All five rows ran in fresh disposable overlays on f44/d69, starting 2026-11-08 19:46 UTC. All five overlays were guarded-retired and all campaign wall tiles/tunnels removed by 20:34 UTC.', '', '**Exit pass\*** required a VM setup correction: Fedora/Ubuntu Budgie used the distro `clipman` package, and Omarchy used the distro `wl-clip-persist` package. The process was owned only for this cell; Clipman history lived on tmpfs and was removed. All five stock goldens failed clipboard persistence after explicit Quit, giving **12 pass / 1 fail / 0 not-run per stock row**, or **60 / 5 / 0** total. Independent ordinary foreground `wl-copy` controls also lost text on owner exit. With the manager, independent `wl-paste` retained the exact URL two seconds after Quit and after restart; `/proc` and the socket confirmed the resident had exited. Published put.gd is unchanged; users without a clipboard manager retain this stock limitation.', '', '**Window/desktop pass†** means desktop pixels matched the independent frozen framebuffer exactly, and window capture reported `window_unavailable` with the documented missing `ext-foreign-toplevel-image-capture-source-manager-v1` reason on labwc 0.9 (Fedora44 and Ubuntu26). Fedora45 labwc0.20 and both Hyprland rows captured the fullscreen external fixture window with exact pixels.', '', '**Exact build:** published `v26.1108.4234-nightly`, version `26.1108.4234-nightly`, clean commit `2b5e1b2d3c11757f805331e4104eb06b2c79ad5c`, tree `33b8f29b0a44ec5c0dc37d154cc0938d3612d328`, count4234. Release was published 2026-11-08 17:43 UTC. The worktree and builder clones are based on origin/nightly2b5; harness draft #1314 remains at `c155c3ec855aa69bdb7b49b07081847fe013af65`. No product change or new PR was needed. Every row retains VM/golden identity, exact package checksum and binary hashes, build/capability observations, commands/script snapshots, functional artifacts, original failures and cleanup receipts.', '', '| Run | Host | Profile | Exact published package | SHA-256 |', '|---|---|---|---|---|']
